2. The Professional Mandate: Operational Roles and Strategic Staffing
No Governor can maintain a dominion through solitary effort; maximizing Mojo and commercial throughput requires delegating authority to specialized professionals. Strategic staffing ensures that a club's treasury remains secure while its storefronts perform at peak capacity.
Operational Role Differentiators
The Manager (Commercial Strategy) Managers oversee administrative oversight, adjusting shop commission rates and monitoring inventory logs. Their presence provides a Staff Training buff, increasing the success rate of complex genetic procedures. They also receive redistributed $VBV via the Token-Sink Router.
Security (Defensive Operations) Tasked with protecting the Treasury, Security personnel deploy hardware traps like Laser Tripwires and Sentry Turrets. They manage Bio-Guard Dogs, which jail the rarest card of any failed infiltrator. They are essential for deploying Cyber-Locks (24hr audit prevention) and Cyber-Counters (identifying unauthorized auditors).
The Clerk (Revenue Optimization) Clerks are the engines of turnover. Their primary mandate is to accelerate store turnover speeds, ensuring storefronts process transactions at maximum velocity to build organizational Mojo and optimize revenue flow.
The "EXECUTIVE_PAY" Milestone
Professional roles offer a pathway to "Master Tier" benefits for players without territory. Signing an employment contract worth 500 $VBV or more triggers the EXECUTIVE_PAY achievement, granting role-gated access to premium gear:
Cyber-Locks: Encrypts treasury data to prevent Cyber-Audits for 24 hours.
Cyber-Counters: A single-use defense that reveals the identity of an auditor.
Intel Reports: Crucial data for assessing heist targets or market sentiment.
Rule Breakers: Premium items that allow for strategic advantages, interacting with the "Same" and "Plus" rules on the combat grid.
Insolvency & Professional Safety
To prevent "timing exploits," the Arena utilizes Insolvency Protection. If an employer club dissolves or defaults, contracts terminate automatically, and the player reverts to Freelancer status.
Operational success ultimately feeds into the most volatile currency in the Arena: Reputation.
