3. Reputation as Capital: Market Manipulation and Social Standing
In the Arena, Reputation is a live ecosystem input that directly dictates asset valuation. The symbiotic relationship between social standing and share pricing ensures market value is driven by performance rather than raw capital alone. Critically, increasing Reputation is the only way to unlock additional deck slots in the Deck Manager.
The Rumor Mill Mechanics
Players manipulate market sentiment via the Rumor Mill for a base cost of 500 $VBV. This action is subject to a 20% Regional Governor Tax (100 $VBV) distributed to district leaders. Positive rumors pump asset prices, while negative rumors drive them down.
Anti-Whale Dynamics
The Entity Market uses an Anti-Whale AMM protected by Quadratic Slippage. As order volume increases, the slippage penalty accelerates exponentially. This makes massive, market-altering trades cost-prohibitive, forcing "whales" to use the Rumor Mill or rely on merit-based valuation (match wins) to drive price.
